<title>USA: Seagate Technology debt issue increased.</title>
<headline>Seagate Technology debt issue increased.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagate Technology Inc's planned multi-tranche debt issue was increased in size by $50 million to total $500 million on Thursday, according to lead manager Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>The seven-year tranche will take the entire increase for a new total of $200 million, the dealer said. The deal will also include $150 million 10-year debt and $150 million 40-year bonds with a 12 year put option.</p>
<p>A formal pricing is expected on Thursday, sources said. The deal is rated Baa3 by Moody's Investors Service and BBB by Standard &amp; Poor's.</p>
<p>((--Al Yoon, 212-859-1672))</p>
